# IDOR and query scoping

## Package recommendation

Prevent insecure direct object references: never trust request IDs alone. Authorize access to the loaded resource and prefer identity-aware query scoping where the plugin/project supports it.

## Required behavior

- After `get`/`get()` by primary key, authorize before mutating or exposing sensitive fields.
- Prefer scoped finders/policy scope methods when the app already uses them — inspect first.
- Do not leak existence of unauthorized records via differing error shapes unless project convention requires it.
- Pair with tight `_accessible` / field lists on patch (mass-assignment).

## Anti-patterns

- `get($this->request->getParam('id'))` then edit with no authorization
- Authorization-only-in-UI
- Over-wide `_accessible` to “make authorize work”
